# March of the World Ooze, the other player's side: Bot2 controls it. Bot1 casts a Phyrexian Walker on its own turn 1 (no March yet). On Bot2's turn 2 Bot2
# casts March (Black Lotus and three Moxen) and then a Memnite: casting on its own turn gives no Elephant, and Bot2's creatures are 6/6 Oozes
# while Bot1's Walker is still a 0/3. Bot1 then casts Lightning Bolt at Bot2 on Bot2's turn: "not their turn" is true for Bot1, so Bot2, March's
# controller, creates a 3/3 Elephant that March makes a 6/6 Ooze, and Bot1 gets nothing. Casting the Bolt in response to March itself would not have
# triggered it: March is not yet on the battlefield (CR 603.2 only looks at permanents that were there when the spell was cast).

